Z||000001||biggdaddy||10-08-1999||04:46 PM||||Anyone???||||reg||5
Z||000002||mwbackus||10-08-1999||04:46 PM||||Heres what I would do, in order of preference.<BR>1.  Check your Bios setup to see if it is correctly defining the hard drive criterion.<BR>2.  Boot from a clean (no virus) system disk! Run Fdisk from this floppy, select option 3 (just to see if the system see's a hard drive) dont do a partition or anything else!.<BR>3.  Open the case and reseat the cables on the hard disk and controller, and the power cable to the hard drive.  Listen to see if the drive spins up when booted. <BR>4.  Call Compaq tech support, they have a very good repair program, they even send you a postage paid shipping box for the RPO.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000003||WisconsinGT||10-08-1999||07:18 PM||||Buy a Macintosh!||||reg||1
